    "description": "Web Developer\n•   Battery Coupon Tracking.   Backend data utilized was a SQL Server database housed in the cloud (MS Azure).  Built responsive web application for both narrow & wide viewports enabling tracking of usage of Battery Coupon Deal codes.  \n\n•   Promised Time of Arrival Dashboard.  Built a web application to enable multiple offices across multiple markets to track and manage Promised Time of Arrival (PTA) on road service calls.\n\nTechnologies: Javascript, HTML, CSS, .NET 4.7, .NET Web API, C#, JSON, DataTables.NET, MS Azure.\n\nAngular Developer\n•  Worked on the second-generation Service Performance and Inventory Management System (SPIMS 2) web application.\n\nTechnologies: Angular, Javascript, C#, .NET Web Services, SQL Server.\n\n\nWeb and Full Stack Developer – Auto Club Enterprises (ACE) Common Platform Initiative\n•   Continued to add new services and features to Auto Club’s Intelligent Roadside Assistance System call receiving / intake system on which I have been a primary developer.  Mission-critical application that is a combination Windows and Web written 75% in VB.NET, 25% in C#.\n\n•   Worked with AAA National to establish two-way communication between their dispatching systems and the Intelligent Roadside Assistance System (IRAS).\n\n•   Updated the Mapping and Geolocation feature of the call intake system to support Google Mapping API.  Also Integrated the system with Yellow Pages, Hertz / Enterprise, and Lyft restful Web Services.  Utilized my skills in graphics and facility with graphic design tools like Photoshop to create icons for the user interface.\n\nTechnologies:  C#, VB.NET, HTML, Javascript, MS SQL Server, CSS, JSON, XML, RESTful and SOAP Services, WinForms.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nOther organizations I have done W2 Contract software engineering work for\n\n•   Mercury Insurance\n•   San Diego City Employees Retirement\n•   Advisys (formerly Kettley Publishing)\n•   Ceridian Tax Service\n•   Taco Bell Corp HQ",
